			<div class="content" id="post-content-1758492">
									

<blockquote>
<p>matter cannot come closer than 1&#160;cm of the walls, floor, ceiling, and supports.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So&#8230; the explorator actually floated over the wreck?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>D-7569 is a 37-year old Caucasian male with a height of 90&#160;cm</p>
</blockquote>
<p>He's rather short, isn't he?</p>
<blockquote>
<p><em>Video feed confirms D-7569's claim, the tentacle appears to be protruding from a mass of human remains, approximately 20 meteres</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>Spelling error.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><em>D-5769 starts screaming, approximately 10 meters above the mass.</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>So, who's that? :)</p>
<blockquote>
<p><em>which indicate that D-7569 is entrapped by the entity's tentacles.</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>Sounds somehow wrong to me as you haven't noticed an entity up to this point.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><em>This is an excerpt from a journal in the possession of the ship's captain</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>Was this found on the island or somewhere within the ship? Because you didn't mention any bodies and I would think the journal would be impossible to remove if it &quot;belonged&quot; tho the wreck because of the barrier (see above).</p>
<p>Also, I would recommend giving the vessel a nice and spooky name and adding more details about the anomaly.</p>

